Contents vendored
-----------------
  dp/        The C data-plane daemon (~30k LOC). Performs in-line packet
             inspection via NFQUEUE or AF_PACKET, runs DPI parsers for
             HTTP/DNS/MySQL/Postgres/Redis/Kafka/gRPC/SSL/SSH/etc., maintains
             per-session byte/packet counters, and emits DPMsgConnect /
             DPMsgThreatLog records back to the agent over a Unix socket.

  base.h     Shared C macros (FLAGS_TEST, FLAGS_SET, byte order, …).
             Referenced by dp/Makefile.rule via `-include ../base.h`.

  defs.h     Wire-format definitions for the agent ↔ dp IPC protocol:
             DPMsgHdr, DPMsgConnect, DPMsgSession, DPMsgThreatLog, etc.
             Referenced via `-include ../defs.h`.

  LICENSE    Apache License 2.0 (NeuVector upstream).

Why a verbatim copy
-------------------
A clean fork keeps `git diff` against neuvector/main legible and lets us
absorb upstream CVE / performance patches with a low-friction rebase.
No code in this tree should be modified except via the sync procedure in
./README.md; downstream behavior changes belong in
constellation/internal/runtime/dp/ (the Go supervisor and IPC consumer
that consumes the wire formats defined here).

Modifications
-------------
None — files are byte-for-byte identical to the upstream revision listed
above. Build artifacts (.objs/, .deps/, *.o, *.d, compile_commands.json)
are excluded from the vendor.

